{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Two follow-ups to the 3045 Verified -1:\n1. Prerequisite workflow-only change pushed: Gerrit 3048 \"Guard the MCP model drift step for its removal\" (wraps the step in the ee2a if-present guard; make verify on it: 17 failures, all the known arm64 pandoc host defect). Once it merges, 3045 is rebased and re-pushed, and this ticket is re-reviewed against that main (the latest BLOCK was precisely that main's step carries no guard yet).\n2. pip-audit cell: change 3045 edited pyproject.toml (the inert per-file ruff ignore), which makes the Gerrit dependency lane block on the outstanding main advisories tracked by unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis. 3045 now leaves pyproject.toml untouched (amended locally, not yet re-pushed); the line's removal is filed as task astrakhan-sylphish-imago (depends_on unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis, discovered_from this story)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792393527354258840,"uuid":"0c0ef6df-3cd7-4754-9214-79357e6853fd"}